{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["Or died, or was broken — that a lion or evil beast tore it apart. For just as 'died' or 'was taken captive' means the entire animal is lost, so too 'broken': the entire animal is destroyed, for a lion or evil beast killed it. For so we find in the case of the prophet: the lion killed both the donkey and the man, and the lion stood by the corpse and neither ate the corpse nor broke the donkey — as it says: ולא אכל האריה את הנבלה ולא כתת את החמור."], :book :exodus, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {0 "Rashbam refers to 1 Kings 13 where a lion kills the disobedient prophet; the Hebrew text here says 'and did not eat the corpse and did not break the donkey,' echoing ולא אכל האריה את הנבלה ולא כתת את החמור (1 Kings 13:28). The final phrase 'אין רואה' is textually uncertain; rendered hyper-literally as 'one does not see' but may be corrupt."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:42:36.296295011Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}